      "sequence_position": 26,
      "problem": "Mina and Sora have the same number of songs in a playlist. A total of $58%$ of Mina's songs are from the 2000s, while $\\frac{13}{20}$ of Sora's songs are from the 2000s. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Sora's songs are from the 2000s. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, she has \n{{field-2}}\nsongs from the 2000s compared to Mina.",
      "worked_solution": "We need to compare $\\frac{13}{20}$ with $58%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{13}{20}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{13}{20}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{20}=\\frac{13\\times 5}{20\\times 5}=\\frac{65}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{65}{100}=65%\n$$\n\nSince $65%>58%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $65%$ of Sora's songs are from the 2000s.\n\n- Therefore, she has $\\text{more}$ songs from the 2000s compared to Mina.",
